cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Who buys online in Spain? Evidence from the INE ICT household survey, 2024"
abstract: >-
  R code that measures online shopping in Spain with the microdata of the INE
  Survey on Equipment and Use of ICT in Households (TIC-H) 2024: weighted
  purchase rates by population group and a weighted binary logit model for
  employees, with average marginal effects, delta-method standard errors and
  predictive performance.
authors:
  - family-names: "Mancilla Paucar"
    given-names: "Dax Kevin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2070-996X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/daxmancilla/online-shopping-spain-INE"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
keywords:
  - e-commerce
  - binary choice model
  - logit
  - survey data
  - INE
  - R
  - Spain
